<item>
            <title>[LU-20713] lease lock leak during migrate</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20713</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68709&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68709&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;mdt_migrate_close() is only called from mdt_reint_migrate() on the&lt;br/&gt;
success path (after the source open_sem has been taken). If the&lt;br/&gt;
migration later fails - e.g. the directory is already being migrated&lt;br/&gt;
and the source lookup returns -EALREADY, or mdo_migrate() errors out -&lt;br/&gt;
the server-side close of the file that carries the lease is skipped&lt;br/&gt;
altogether.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The client considers the migrate close done and has already canceled&lt;br/&gt;
its lease lock, so the server-side lease is never revoked either.&lt;br/&gt;
As a result the file stays open on the MDT and its locks are only&lt;br/&gt;
cleaned up on reclaim, keeping the file busy (e.g. for HSM release or&lt;br/&gt;
future migration) and leaking the server-side lock until then.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
